// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HEROES OF MIGHT AND MAGIC: A STRATEGIC QUEST
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Roadmap checklist (via perchance.org/atomic-roadmap).
// Work is done ONE task at a time: pick the first uncompleted task,
// implement it, mark it [x], and stop for review.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Phase 0: Branding
// 1. [x] Project branding: set the game name, build the title screen, and ship a heraldic logo banner.

// Phase 1: World Map & Exploration
// 2. [x] Map Generation: Generate a coordinate-based grid map containing randomized terrain types, resource nodes (Gold, Gems), and static encounter markers.
// 3. [x] Hero Movement: Implement a movement system where a hero entity moves one tile per turn; movement is blocked by impassable terrain.
// 4. [x] Fog of War: Implement a visibility system that hides map tiles and entities until the hero enters a defined radius of the tile.
// 5. [x] Resource Collection: Implement a mechanism to trigger a resource gain event when a hero moves onto a resource node, removing the node from the map.
// 6. [x] Encounter Trigger: Implement a state transition that switches the app from "Map View" to "Battle View" when a hero moves onto an enemy entity.

// Phase 2: Army & Unit Management
// 7. [x] Army Composition: Create a data structure to track multiple unit types, their current count, and their base stats (Attack, Defense, Health).
// 8. [x] Unit Recruitment: Implement a function to add units to the army based on a gold cost and availability at specific map locations.
// 9. [x] Army Capacity: Establish a maximum unit limit per slot and a total army size limit for the hero.
// 10. [x] Unit Casualty Tracking: Implement a system to permanently reduce unit counts based on losses sustained during combat.

// Phase 3: Turn-Based Combat System
// 11. [x] Combat Grid Layout: Create a distinct combat screen with a fixed grid where friendly and enemy units are positioned based on their recruitment order.
// 12. [x] Turn Order Logic: Implement a combat sequence based on a "Speed" attribute, determining which unit acts first.
// 13. [x] Attack Resolution: Create a formula to calculate damage based on Attacker's Attack vs. Defender's Defense, reducing the Defender's current Health.
// 14. [x] Unit Death Logic: Implement a check to remove a unit from the grid once Health reaches zero, shifting remaining units forward if applicable.
// 15. [x] Victory/Defeat Conditions: Implement a check to return to the Map View and distribute rewards (XP, Gold) when all enemies are defeated or the hero is wiped out.

// Phase 4: Hero Progression & Skills
// 16. [x] Hero Attribute System: Implement a system to track Hero stats (Attack, Defense, Spell Power, Knowledge) and current Level.
// 17. [x] XP Gain & Level Up: Create a logic gate that increments Hero Level when an XP threshold is reached, allowing the user to select one attribute to increase.
// 18. [x] Ability Triggering: Implement a system for "Special Abilities" (e.g., Area Attack) that targets multiple units based on a specific cost or cooldown.

// Phase 5: UI & State Persistence
// 19. [x] Global State Manager: Implement a centralized state to track Hero stats, Army composition, and Map progress across different views.
// 20. [x] HUD Implementation: Create a persistent UI overlay showing current Gold, Army size, and current Hero level during exploration.
// 21. [x] Save/Load System: Implement a mechanism to export and import the current game state as a string to allow session persistence.

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title
  Heroes of Might and Magic: A Strategic Quest

$meta
  title = Heroes of Might and Magic: A Strategic Quest
  description = A complete recreation of the classic 1995 turn-based strategy game — command heroes, gather armies, and conquer the realm.
  tags = strategy, game, heroes, turn-based, adventure
  header
    mode = minimal
